[1m[38;5;231mWhich logging architecture should the spec be built around?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mA: Black-box recorder (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mRing-buffer breadcrumbs in memory; ship an envelope only when an error fires. Cost tracks failures, not traffic.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m B: Buffered log stream
     [38;5;246mUniform record queue, periodic + threshold + unload flush. Supports aggregate analysis; transmits for healthy [39m
     [38;5;246msessions too.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m C: Immediate per-record POST
     [38;5;246mNo buffer, one request per record. Smallest code; does not scale and drops on failure.[39m
